 "result": "Methods of `Config` in `src/tessel/config.py` (a `dict` subclass):\n\n- `__init__` (L94): creates the config with a `root_path` for resolving relative files and optional default values.\n- `from_envvar` (L102): loads a Python config file whose path is in the named environment variable, with a clear error or silent `False` if it's unset.\n- `load_env_prefixed` (L126): loads `TESSEL_*` environment variables into the config, stripping the prefix, parsing values with `json.loads` by default, and supporting nested keys via `__`.\n- `from_pyfile` (L187): executes a Python file and copies its uppercase names into the config.\n- `from_object` (L218): copies uppercase attributes from an object or import-string module or class into the config.\n- `from_file` (L256): loads a file (JSON, TOML and so on) with a caller-supplied `load` callable and passes the mapping to `from_mapping`.\n- `from_mapping` (L304): updates the config from a mapping and keyword args, keeping only uppercase keys, and always returns `True`.\n- `get_namespace` (L323): returns a dict of the options sharing a prefix, optionally trimming the prefix and lowercasing keys.\n- `__repr__` (L366): returns `<Config {...}>`.\n\nThe same file also defines `ConfigAttribute`, a descriptor that forwards attribute access to `obj.config[name]`, but it isn't a method of `Config`.",
